      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While historical data exists, using demographic profiles to weight perceived risk is often ethically problematic and can lead to discriminatory outcomes. A truly robust security AI should prioritize behavioral anomalies, such as unusually slow movement or loitering near entry points, over static demographic identifiers. Focusing solely on behavior allows the system to flag suspicious *actions* universally, preventing the reinforcement of biased patterns found in historical arrest data.",
